GLOSS = r'''
Account lockout|A policy-controlled restriction after failed authentication; it can arise from attack traffic or stale saved credentials.
Access token|A credential granting a client a defined resource scope for a limited lifetime.
Amcache|A Windows artifact that may contain executable and program metadata, subject to OS and collection caveats.
App consent|An authorization decision granting a client application requested scopes or permissions.
ASN|Autonomous System Number that identifies an internet routing organization, not an individual attacker.
Audit blind window|An interval during which expected logs were not collected or retained, limiting negative conclusions.
Baseline cohort|A peer group of similar users, servers or workloads used to interpret anomalous behavior.
Canary event|A deliberately produced benign test event used to confirm that collection and detection function.
Case attribution|The evidence-supported link between an event and an identity, device, process or business activity.
Certificate template|An Active Directory Certificate Services definition controlling issuance requirements and enrollment rights.
Cloud data event|An audit record for object-level or workload data operations, when supported and enabled.
Correlation key|A stable identifier used to link related events across systems, such as session or process GUID.
Credential replay|Use of an existing credential or token in another session, not necessarily requiring password knowledge.
Detection blind spot|A behavior or environment condition not covered by available telemetry or detection logic.
Detection SLO|An agreed quantitative target for log freshness, alert latency or known-positive detection reliability.
Device compliance|A management assessment of endpoint policy state, not proof that its user session is trustworthy.
DMARC alignment|Match requirements between visible From domain and SPF or DKIM-authenticated domain identities.
Domain fronting|Routing traffic via shared infrastructure where network-level names and backend destination may differ.
Effective permission|What an identity can actually do after combining roles, policy and resource access controls.
Event 4698|Windows Security auditing event for scheduled task creation when applicable audit settings are enabled.
Event 4740|Windows Security auditing event indicating an account was locked out.
Event 4887|Windows CA auditing event for a certificate request approved and certificate issued, when enabled.
Event 5136|Directory Service Changes auditing event for directory object modifications when configured.
Field drift|A change in normalized field names or types that can break searches or detections.
Fingerprint collision risk|The limitation of treating a coarse fingerprint shared by many clients as a unique identity.
Golden Ticket|An adversarial forged Kerberos TGT concept; detection requires multiple correlated observations.
Host path|A Kubernetes volume mechanism mounting files from a cluster node into a pod.
Immutability|A retention property that prevents unauthorized alteration of saved evidence under defined controls.
Ingestion time|When a collector receives an event, which can differ significantly from when it happened.
Known negative|A benign fixture expected not to trigger a particular detection.
Known positive|A controlled behavioral fixture expected to trigger a particular detection.
Logon ID|A locally scoped Windows session identifier useful for linking associated security events.
OAuth scope|A named permission requested by a client to access a resource or API.
Out-of-band verification|Contact using an independently trusted channel, separate from the potentially compromised message or session.
Process GUID|A process identifier that can be more stable than a recycled numeric PID within its producer's scope.
Query cardinality|The number of distinct values or joins considered, affecting cost and false correlation risk.
Refresh token|A credential that can obtain new access tokens under server controls, often outliving one access token.
Response decision log|A timestamped record of operational decisions, approvers, trade-offs and follow-up checkpoints.
Session issuer|The role or original identity responsible for creating an assumed-role session in cloud identity systems.
Source identity|A provenance indicator passed into certain cloud role sessions; inspect its trust and enforcement rules.
Suppression blast radius|The range of alerts and assets excluded by a detection exception.
Telemetry parity|Comparable security observability across protocols, operating systems, regions and deployment types.
Time-to-detect|Duration from relevant observable behavior to actionable alert or analyst recognition.
Token family|A set of linked auth/session tokens issued under a shared client or session context, where vendor data permits.
Triage pivot|A specific next evidence search linked to an observed entity, signal or hypothesis.
WinRM|Windows Remote Management, a legitimate administration channel that can also be abused for remote execution.
'''.strip()
existing={x['term'].casefold() for x in d['glossary']}
for line in GLOSS.splitlines():
    term,definition=line.split('|')
    if term.casefold() not in existing:
      d['glossary'].append({'term':term,'definition':definition});existing.add(term.casefold())

ATLAS = r'''
Windows|4740|Account locked out|Correlate caller computer, target user and prior failed logons; status alone does not identify attacker.|4625, VPN activity, password changes
Windows|4698|Scheduled task registered|Task creation requires principal, action and trigger context to distinguish automation from persistence.|4702, Task Scheduler Operational, EDR parent process
Windows|5136|Directory object modified|With Directory Service Changes audit enabled, reconstruct attribute and owner changes, especially delegation and group ACLs.|5137, 4662, object before/after state
Windows|4887|Certificate issued|CA issuance event can support investigation of unusual authentication certificates; logging must be enabled.|4886, requester, template, certificate serial
Windows|7045|New service installed|System log service-install evidence; examine image path, service identity, source admin logon and change approval.|4624, 4672, process chain
Windows|4104|PowerShell script block|Script block recording depends on policy; code fragments may be benign admin scripts.|4103, EDR command line, file writes
Network|DHCP LEASE|Endpoint attribution|IP ownership can change; resolve host and user to the exact UTC interval.|VPN address pool, NAC, NAT translation
Network|DNS NXDOMAIN|Failed DNS resolution|Frequency and unusual domains are leads, not independent proof of command and control.|Endpoint process, DNS qtype, deployment changes
Cloud|STS ASSUME ROLE|Assumed cloud identity|Trace original caller, role trust, source identity and downstream actions across accounts.|CloudTrail userIdentity, session issuer, accessKeyId
Cloud|S3 DATA EVENT|Object read audit|Reads indicate access under collection policy, not necessarily external transfer.|S3 data events, CloudTrail, proxy egress
Cloud|AUDIT SELECTOR|Collection configuration|A trail's event selectors decide which data calls are collected; disablement creates blind windows.|PutEventSelectors, organization trail health
Identity|OAUTH CONSENT|App grant|App permissions may enable persistent API access; investigate requester, publisher and scope.|Entra audit, app registration, resource activity
Detection|CANARY|Known-positive test event|A repeatable control helps detect parser or scheduling regressions before production incidents are missed.|Raw/normalized field mapping, alert latency
Detection|FIELD NULL RATE|Schema health signal|A sudden rise in missing normalized fields can silently break rules after parser or source changes.|Collector versions, raw events, test fixtures
Kubernetes|POD CREATE|Pod admission|Privilege settings and service-account identity help identify unexpected access to node resources.|kube-audit, RBAC, admission controller
Kubernetes|SECRET GET|Secret access request|Reads should be correlated with service account workloads, namespace and approval, not assumed hostile.|kube-audit, RBAC bindings, workload identity
'''.strip()
atlas_set={(x['category'],x['code']) for x in d['atlas']}
for line in ATLAS.splitlines():
    category,code,title,description,pivots=line.split('|')
    if (category,code) not in atlas_set:
      d['atlas'].append(dict(category=category,code=code,title=title,description=description,pivots=pivots))

QUERIES = [
 ('KQL','Process ancestry: suspicious child','DeviceProcessEvents\n| where Timestamp > ago(24h)\n| where InitiatingProcessFileName =~ "winword.exe"\n| project Timestamp,DeviceName,FileName,ProcessCommandLine,InitiatingProcessFileName','Defender XDR table/fields must be available; investigate child lineage rather than assuming maliciousness.'),
 ('KQL','Endpoint network pivot','DeviceNetworkEvents\n| where Timestamp > ago(24h)\n| where RemotePort == 443\n| summarize Connections=count() by DeviceName,InitiatingProcessFileName,RemoteUrl','Group egress by process and host; validate URL availability and shared CDN context.'),
 ('KQL','Uncommon service account device','DeviceLogonEvents\n| where Timestamp > ago(7d)\n| where AccountName has "svc"\n| summarize Devices=dcount(DeviceName),Hosts=make_set(DeviceName,20) by AccountName','Use organization-specific identity classification and expected workload host inventory.'),
 ('KQL','Suspicious email rule activity','CloudAppEvents\n| where Timestamp > ago(7d)\n| where ActionType has "Inbox"\n| project Timestamp,AccountDisplayName,ActionType,RawEventData','The connector’s ActionType values may differ; inspect real schemas before production deployment.'),
 ('KQL','Device process rarity','DeviceProcessEvents\n| where Timestamp > ago(14d)\n| summarize HostCount=dcount(DeviceName),Occurrences=count() by FileName\n| where HostCount < 3','Rarity only builds a hunt lead; combine with signer, parent and actual business role.'),
 ('KQL','Cloud control plane change','AzureActivity\n| where TimeGenerated > ago(7d)\n| where OperationNameValue has_any ("write","delete")\n| project TimeGenerated,Caller,ResourceId,OperationNameValue,ActivityStatusValue','Illustrative Azure Activity query; narrow with resource type and approved deployment records.'),
 ('SPL','Account lockout investigation','index=wineventlog EventCode=4740 earliest=-48h\n| stats count by TargetUserName, CallerComputerName\n| sort - count','Field names are TA-dependent; correlate 4625 and password reset windows.'),
 ('SPL','New services by host','index=windows sourcetype="WinEventLog:System" EventCode=7045 earliest=-7d\n| stats values(ServiceName) as services count by host\n| sort - count','Service installs can be routine; pair with management tools and binary provenance.'),
 ('SPL','DNS outliers by host','index=dns earliest=-24h\n| stats dc(query) as unique_queries count by src\n| sort - unique_queries','Unique DNS labels can reflect legitimate software; compare cohort baseline and process telemetry.'),
 ('SPL','Check SIEM collection drift','index=_internal source=*metrics.log* group=per_sourcetype_thruput earliest=-24h\n| timechart span=1h sum(kb) by series','Internal metrics availability and labels depend on Splunk deployment; use to detect ingestion drops.'),
 ('SPL','New scheduled tasks','index=windows EventCode=4698 earliest=-7d\n| table _time host SubjectUserName TaskName TaskContent\n| sort - _time','Enable relevant Windows audit policy; correlate task XML, process and owner approval.'),
 ('SPL','Correlate privileged group changes','index=windows (EventCode=4728 OR EventCode=4732 OR EventCode=4756) earliest=-7d\n| stats count values(MemberName) as members by host TargetUserName SubjectUserName','Audit scope and parser field names vary; tie to ticketed group membership changes.'),
]
